Rule 1 (input and target must have identical shapes)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ (if ndim(v_1) ≥ 1 then ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i))
>>
Rule 3 (eps must be positive and small)
{v_1 : float} |= v_1 > 0 ∧ v_1 ≤ 1
>>
Rule 4 (when log_input is False, eps must be strictly positive)
{v_1 : bool, v_2 : float} |= if v_1 = false then v_2 > 0
>>
Rule 5 (valid reduction mode)
{v_1 : str} |= v_1 = "none" ∨ v_1 = "mean" ∨ v_1 = "sum"
>>
Rule 6 (no zero-sized dimensions in inputs to avoid size mismatches)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) ≥ 1 ∧ ndim(v_2) ≥ 1 then (∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) > 0) ∧ (∀j ∈ [0, ndim(v_2) - 1] : shape(v_2, j) > 0)
